    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:b7ea319726e505ba",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "7380d3d00c2d2a36a355ffc0601472e6cc06d1c8993993cb2cd29528fc39d190",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. The included group sightseeing tour of Santiago is led by an English-speaking guide."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:92b8569c9fae9604",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "c0d4084e6d8965895023a8e7046be99b2b1d39143ab727c9b0d6599e03cfd931",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Join an English-speaking guide for a group sightseeing tour of Santiago. You will start in the city centre at the square by La Moneda Palace, a designated historic monument. Built in 1799 during the final years of Spanish rule, this neoclassical building was originally intended to house the Royal Mint. It became the seat of the Chilean government in the mid-19th century and has served that role ever since. Continue to Plaza de Armas, Santiago’s main square and the site where the city’s history began. Around the square are the former residence of the governors of Chile, Santiago City Hall, the Central Post Office, the Royal Court building and the Metropolitan Cathedral. You will then climb Santa Lucía Hill for a panoramic view of the city. The tour continues through the modern districts of Vitacura, Las Condes and Providencia, with a drive along the Mapocho River and a look at the architecture lining Santiago’s main avenues."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:ef5bf6affbc74add",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8411760284e634c6f3e3bff2f9249955104e1e872b20ce0f3ea4b116c2f75953",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9om5vj-qfbonkk",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "For an additional charge, you can visit wineries in the Maipo Valley for a tasting. The price is $230 per person, with a minimum of 2 participants."
    },
